00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:07.520
You're going to move.

00:29:09.190 --> 00:29:10.050
I don't think so.

00:29:11.370 --> 00:29:12.930
At least not for a while yet anyway.

00:29:14.200 --> 00:29:16.700
I keep hoping I'll find some clue.

00:29:16.950 --> 00:29:17.670
Oh, that remote.

00:29:18.430 --> 00:29:19.410
Can't stay here very well.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:23.290
My assistant, Quigley's, please.

00:29:27.390 --> 00:29:27.770
Thanks, Howard.

00:29:28.750 --> 00:29:29.970
Has now reported they arrived here.

00:29:52.370 --> 00:29:57.290
I don't know, two or three of them, we got a chance, let's go.

00:30:37.290 --> 00:30:39.050
We're standing right in the middle of Main Street here.

00:30:39.660 --> 00:30:40.080
Wait a minute.

00:30:40.180 --> 00:30:41.480
I wonder what's inside these.

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:42.940
Let's look.

00:30:46.130 --> 00:30:46.730
More important.

00:30:48.110 --> 00:30:48.290
Yeah.

00:30:51.930 --> 00:30:52.730
Some kind of shirt.

00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:54.220
Uniform shirt.

00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:56.220
Fancy dress costumes and everything.

00:30:57.090 --> 00:30:57.590
Even buttons.

00:30:58.100 --> 00:30:58.280
Hell.

00:30:58.610 --> 00:30:58.950
Souvenir.

00:31:00.920 --> 00:31:02.960
Somebody must be making a lot of money out of these things.

00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:04.220
You mean they sell these uniforms?

00:31:04.890 --> 00:31:05.450
They don't get them.

00:31:06.380 --> 00:31:11.940
If you want to play crusader, you've got to buy a uniform, badges, belts, all that organization.

00:31:13.910 --> 00:31:16.240
Wars are warehouse.

00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:18.140
Who do you really think is behind these crusaders?

00:31:21.550 --> 00:31:22.050
They're down there.

00:32:00.380 --> 00:32:00.820
Where'd you get it?

00:32:00.860 --> 00:32:02.020
In a little print shop downtown.

00:32:02.720 --> 00:32:04.300
I haven't watched 24 hours a day.

00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:05.280
Tending to that, boss.

00:32:21.430 --> 00:32:25.370
Mother Hartley, speak for your supper?

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:44.930
Can I send you in?

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:54.100
Mr. Malloy.

00:32:54.240 --> 00:32:56.960
Mr. Malloy.

00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:03.260
So glad you could drop by.

00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:05.660
Frankly, your call aroused my curiosity.

00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:06.540
Lucid.

00:33:07.170 --> 00:33:07.430
Thanks.

00:33:09.650 --> 00:33:11.740
Howard, may I call you Howard?

00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:13.040
Yes, of course.

00:33:14.280 --> 00:33:15.960
You want to be special prosecutor?

00:33:17.280 --> 00:33:17.540
Huh?

00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:20.710
Because you can be if you want to be.

00:33:21.080 --> 00:33:24.600
Some rather influential people think you're the man for the job.

00:33:25.160 --> 00:33:26.740
Well, Charlie Riggs started it.

00:33:27.220 --> 00:33:28.300
I'd like a chance to finish it.

00:33:28.380 --> 00:33:29.920
They've already been in touch with a guy.

00:33:33.020 --> 00:33:36.380
Frank, he won't object when he knows that I'm supporting you.

00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:37.800
I'm very grateful.

00:33:38.780 --> 00:33:39.520
Now, one thing.

00:33:40.400 --> 00:33:43.380
I'm told that a small-time politician named Agostini

00:33:44.280 --> 00:33:47.580
had something to do with suggesting your name a special prosecutor.

00:33:49.370 --> 00:33:50.350
That's right, he did.

00:33:50.780 --> 00:33:55.020
But this man's reputation is unsavory, to say the least.

00:33:55.440 --> 00:33:58.500
I suggest that you disavow Mr. Agostini immediately.

00:33:58.500 --> 00:33:58.820
Thank you.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:09.480
disavow. In that case, I think you might consider yourself appointed. Malloy, try to reach you all

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:16.080
afternoon. Other people can call you a special prosecutor. To me, you'll always be my favorite

00:34:16.080 --> 00:34:29.790
assistant. That you, Malloy? Agostini. I fall to congratulate you on your appointment. Anything I can do,

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:30.490
Let me know.

00:34:31.830 --> 00:34:32.770
Call me Angel.

00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:38.600
Your special prosecutor.

00:34:40.700 --> 00:34:42.450
I expect a great thing to love you.

00:34:43.090 --> 00:34:46.160
By the way, could you drive over tomorrow night?

00:34:46.420 --> 00:34:47.680
I want you to meet some people.

00:34:48.250 --> 00:34:51.760
I've sent you a confidential file on some of them.

00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:54.340
Men who have tremendous influence.

00:34:55.610 --> 00:34:57.670
Take a look at my notes before you come over.

00:34:58.350 --> 00:34:58.610
Yeah.

00:34:59.180 --> 00:34:59.920
Yeah, I'll do that.

00:35:00.570 --> 00:35:01.370
About 6 tomorrow?

00:35:01.960 --> 00:35:02.340
Right.

00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:07.360
Mrs. Hartley sent you this envelope about an hour ago by special message.

00:35:07.600 --> 00:35:08.680
Yeah, she just told me.

00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:14.330
Things are moving pretty fast, aren't they?

00:35:14.430 --> 00:35:15.340
Yeah, sir.

00:35:17.190 --> 00:35:19.110
I wish there was something I could do to help you, Howard.

00:35:23.450 --> 00:35:25.150
I usually like that myself.

00:35:34.740 --> 00:35:36.650
But what about these wires?

00:35:37.740 --> 00:35:38.980
All these papers you have to...

00:35:38.980 --> 00:35:43.360
I could run errands.

00:35:43.520 --> 00:35:45.180
I hate to keep you out of this, sweetie.

00:35:46.060 --> 00:35:48.500
Howard, we picked her up at the airport.

00:35:48.910 --> 00:35:50.010
Sonny, I have no right to stop.

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:50.920
Where were you going?

00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:52.300
Get a one-way ticket to Mexico City.

00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:53.380
I take a little trip.

00:35:53.940 --> 00:35:54.260
Expensive.

00:35:54.600 --> 00:35:55.060
Who arranged it?

00:35:55.220 --> 00:35:55.540
Nobody.

00:35:56.160 --> 00:35:57.160
Somebody ordered you to leave.

00:35:57.360 --> 00:35:57.760
Who was it?

00:35:58.420 --> 00:35:58.640
Please.

00:35:59.480 --> 00:35:59.960
I have had...

00:36:00.410 --> 00:36:04.620
much trouble. Without my husband, I don't know what to do.

00:36:04.800 --> 00:36:10.020
Mrs. Quietius, what is it? Someone called it this afternoon, told her to catch the next

00:36:10.020 --> 00:36:13.380
plane to Mexico City. You know about that? We've had your telephone tapped for several

00:36:13.380 --> 00:36:23.280
days. Please, for your own sake. I don't know. It was a voice.

00:36:24.190 --> 00:36:29.900
Booker is a material. This means you'll be safe, Mrs. If we let you go home, those men might

00:36:30.030 --> 00:36:35.350
kill you the way they killed your husband. Come along, Mrs. Barr. Don't you worry. Mr. Malloy will

00:36:35.350 --> 00:36:51.670
take good care of you, won't you? What a hell. Hey, you got the job. I wanted you to say that. I did.

00:36:52.590 --> 00:36:58.570
Anything else you wanted me to say? Anything else you want to say? That'd take a long. Oh.

00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:01.920
Thank you.

00:37:35.070 --> 00:37:38.240
Yes, dear. You've come, I'm so free.

00:37:38.420 --> 00:37:40.250
So am I. Change the scene.

00:37:40.840 --> 00:37:41.720
Will you have a cocktail?

00:37:42.020 --> 00:37:43.620
Or would you rather have something to drink?

00:37:44.640 --> 00:37:45.560
Thanks, I'll wait up one.

00:37:46.680 --> 00:37:47.660
Well, just as you please.

00:37:49.280 --> 00:37:54.700
Now, I told you, I'm going to meet some people.

00:37:55.050 --> 00:37:56.690
Grace, will you come over and look at this?

00:37:56.930 --> 00:37:57.850
Presently, my dear.

00:37:58.620 --> 00:37:59.960
Some people who were there...

00:38:02.080 --> 00:38:03.640
I've met a few of those already.

00:38:03.840 --> 00:38:04.960
We'll add to your collection.

00:38:06.050 --> 00:38:06.810
All these people?

00:38:06.950 --> 00:38:07.290
Oh, no.

00:38:07.710 --> 00:38:09.010
Just the ones I sent you to know.

00:38:09.780 --> 00:38:10.160
Doesn't matter.

00:38:10.760 --> 00:38:12.340
I don't know people here myself.

00:38:12.780 --> 00:38:13.340
And thank you.

00:38:14.080 --> 00:38:17.690
The only people I enjoy in these are the ones I haven't met before.

00:38:17.950 --> 00:38:20.190
The strangers that my friends bring along.

00:38:21.190 --> 00:38:21.770
Shall we go?

00:38:24.700 --> 00:38:26.220
You went over my notes carefully.

00:38:26.380 --> 00:38:27.040
Yes, very.

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:34.640
Oh, pardon. As we meet the subject of this...

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:36.080
Grace, I left your cocktail.

00:38:36.500 --> 00:38:37.600
Yes, just a moment.

00:38:41.220 --> 00:38:41.600
Correct.

00:38:42.570 --> 00:38:45.270
Mr. Nichols, may I present Mr. Malloy?

00:38:45.450 --> 00:38:47.530
Harry, this is our new special prosecutor.

00:38:47.710 --> 00:38:47.950
Hello.

00:38:48.290 --> 00:38:49.330
We've already met.

00:38:49.550 --> 00:38:50.030
Formerly.

00:38:50.170 --> 00:38:52.210
Mr. Nichols' papers didn't think much of my appointment.

00:38:52.880 --> 00:38:54.050
Harry, against you?

00:38:54.360 --> 00:38:54.500
Really?

00:38:55.150 --> 00:38:58.090
Well, surely it's only because he's opposing his local competitor,

00:38:58.860 --> 00:38:59.820
the Express Journal.

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:04.940
Oh, now, really, Grace, who wants to look into a man's motives at a gay time like this?

00:39:06.800 --> 00:39:08.800
A little relaxation from serious things.

00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:26.840
This is the time to discuss Mr. Malloy's business or mine.

00:39:27.040 --> 00:39:29.900
Why, Harry, I thought you did all your business at cocktail parties.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.520
Sometimes, Grace, your polite little jokes aren't very polite.

00:39:32.660 --> 00:39:33.420
Or very little.

00:39:33.880 --> 00:39:35.600
Which brings us to Tom Waldron, Jr.

00:39:36.090 --> 00:39:39.970
Mr. Malloy, may I present the worst-dressed radio executive in the industry

00:39:39.970 --> 00:39:43.340
and the only really frivolous mind you'll meet this afternoon.

00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:48.190
If Grace hadn't been Judge Hartley's wife, she'd not get away with such casual slander.

00:40:01.910 --> 00:40:06.680
If Grace ever runs out of bright conversation,

00:40:06.940 --> 00:40:09.000
all she has to do is to remember the judge's epigrams.

00:40:11.300 --> 00:40:14.320
You are a rascal, Kastrick. Complete rascal.

00:40:14.660 --> 00:40:15.500
I acknowledge it.

00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:18.250
And here's Stuart Pembert, public relations.

00:40:18.370 --> 00:40:18.610
Hello.

00:40:20.170 --> 00:40:22.010
Or should I say private relations?

00:40:22.370 --> 00:40:23.370
You shouldn't, Grace.

00:40:24.300 --> 00:40:28.940
May I introduce Sigmund Kastrick, Tartley, Malloy?

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.890
Mr. Kosterick and I have met.

00:40:34.120 --> 00:40:36.080
We seem to recall our meeting.

00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:40.680
Oh, we must take a few excuses.

00:40:43.140 --> 00:40:46.040
Look here, Malloy, this crusade of yours.

00:40:46.470 --> 00:40:47.250
Tongue-in-cheek, isn't it?

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:52.960
Don't tell me you're the quixotic defender of the rights of men.

00:40:54.270 --> 00:40:55.610
Express journal says you are.

00:40:55.750 --> 00:40:57.190
It's hard to tell what you mean.

00:40:58.240 --> 00:40:59.980
What I mean is you can't be falling for your...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.620
your own publicity.

00:41:01.760 --> 00:41:02.780
I can't help thinking the law.

00:41:03.350 --> 00:41:05.630
It's just a big time fixer.

00:41:06.290 --> 00:41:07.190
He's a fool too.

00:41:07.700 --> 00:41:08.460
Very influential.

00:41:09.760 --> 00:41:10.840
Tell you anything about him.

00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:12.580
Self in conversation.

00:41:16.050 --> 00:41:16.330
To hate.

00:41:16.880 --> 00:41:21.160
Just as inalienable as, as inalienable as the right to free speech.

00:41:21.750 --> 00:41:23.290
You've got to defend that too, you know.

00:41:24.130 --> 00:41:25.650
Inalienable is a very important word.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:28.260
I'm sure it's hard to say on purpose.

00:41:28.990 --> 00:41:29.770
Never mind the reaction.

00:41:31.880 --> 00:41:33.480
I'm talking about the history of man.

00:41:34.560 --> 00:41:37.020
Out of hatred came the triumph of one group over another.

00:41:37.640 --> 00:41:39.160
The elimination of the misfit and the weak.

00:41:40.010 --> 00:41:41.830
The creative evolution of a superior class.

00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:43.460
Don't you see, Malloy?

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:46.460
Out of it came our great industrial civilization.

00:41:47.880 --> 00:41:49.160
And out of it came a war.

00:41:49.630 --> 00:41:50.490
Twenty million dead.

00:41:51.680 --> 00:41:53.940
I feel obliged to interrupt this conversation.

00:41:54.140 --> 00:41:55.820
Will you excuse us, Stuart, please?

00:41:59.330 --> 00:41:59.730
Politics.

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:01.240
A bad man.

00:42:01.460 --> 00:42:01.980
I agree.

00:42:02.320 --> 00:42:04.220
And a man with the habit of victory.

00:42:06.290 --> 00:42:06.670
Tim?

00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:07.620
No, thanks.

00:42:08.490 --> 00:42:11.070
Andrew, bring Mr. Malloy a scotch and...

00:42:11.070 --> 00:42:11.290
Why?

00:42:13.550 --> 00:42:13.870
You...

00:42:14.220 --> 00:42:17.540
You must come over here for a moment just to set the point for us.

00:42:18.280 --> 00:42:20.100
Talently unnecessary to an argument.

00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:20.940
Will you excuse me?

00:42:20.960 --> 00:42:21.340
Of course.

00:42:44.080 --> 00:42:44.740
I'm Barbara.

00:42:47.580 --> 00:42:47.980
Good what?

00:42:49.140 --> 00:42:49.780
Name for you.

00:42:50.590 --> 00:42:52.270
You look as if you ought to be called Barbara.

00:42:52.710 --> 00:42:53.110
Really?

00:42:56.950 --> 00:42:57.950
Scotch and water, sir.

00:43:00.540 --> 00:43:01.260
That was mine.

00:43:01.720 --> 00:43:02.440
Yes, I know.

00:43:03.600 --> 00:43:04.000
Thank you.

00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:07.260
I wonder if your name fits the way you look.

00:43:07.550 --> 00:43:08.510
Malloy is my name.

00:43:08.690 --> 00:43:09.450
Howard Malloy.

00:43:09.910 --> 00:43:10.270
Good.

00:43:11.230 --> 00:43:11.670
Good what?

00:43:12.060 --> 00:43:12.620
Good guessing.

00:43:12.980 --> 00:43:14.140
That's who I thought you were.

00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:15.000
How?

00:43:16.020 --> 00:43:18.520
Everybody here has been talking about you this afternoon.

00:43:19.060 --> 00:43:21.780
And you're the only stranger who looks as if he ought to be called Howard.

00:43:24.360 --> 00:43:26.900
You're a special something or other, aren't you?

00:43:28.290 --> 00:43:29.730
I'll secure you.

00:43:30.540 --> 00:43:39.750
sing yes obviously you ever relax from what singing as often as possible what about the song

00:43:39.750 --> 00:43:48.110
a minute ago that was just for myself i like to do things for myself once in a while doesn't that

00:43:48.110 --> 00:43:56.880
happen often no stop this i never answer questions on an empty stomach i'm hungry too with somebody

00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:59.540
that's a very large question

00:44:00.380 --> 00:44:01.960
I'm not with Harry, anyway.

00:44:02.100 --> 00:44:04.750
I, uh, I like the song, Barbara.

00:44:05.270 --> 00:44:06.430
The song, Harry?

00:44:07.200 --> 00:44:07.860
Thank you.

00:44:08.700 --> 00:44:10.020
Howard, please forgive me.

00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:11.380
Did you finally get a drink?

00:44:11.650 --> 00:44:13.390
Yes, I did, Mrs. Hartley.

00:44:13.510 --> 00:44:13.810
Thank you.

00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:18.460
You've met more strangers today than I have.

00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:22.220
I was just getting a coffee with you.

00:44:22.680 --> 00:44:23.360
Goodness, no.

00:44:24.470 --> 00:44:27.230
Well, our Mr. Pemberton's been looking most progressive.

00:44:30.320 --> 00:44:30.800
I know.

00:44:31.790 --> 00:44:34.930
Your office called, Mr. Malloy, and Mr. Quigley is waiting for you.

00:44:35.030 --> 00:44:36.030
They said it was important.

00:44:36.250 --> 00:44:36.870
Yes, thanks.

00:44:37.680 --> 00:44:38.980
Does that mean you have to go?

00:44:39.160 --> 00:44:39.940
Yes, right away.

00:44:40.750 --> 00:44:43.240
Oh, well, I'll have Andrew fetch a hat.

00:44:45.280 --> 00:44:45.540
Good night.

00:44:48.470 --> 00:44:49.590
Good night, Mr. Malloy.

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:32.360
I just wanted to see you again, so...

00:45:32.610 --> 00:45:33.830
Didn't you want to see me again?

00:45:34.030 --> 00:45:36.310
You're still a man with a lot of questions, aren't you?

00:45:36.450 --> 00:45:38.580
Yeah. Didn't you want to see me again?

00:45:39.270 --> 00:45:39.670
Yes.

00:45:40.650 --> 00:45:41.250
All right, then.

00:45:44.470 --> 00:45:45.390
How did you get my number?

00:45:45.610 --> 00:45:46.790
That's easy, where I work.

00:45:47.640 --> 00:45:48.720
Is everything easy for you?

00:45:49.560 --> 00:45:49.780
No.

00:45:51.730 --> 00:45:52.530
Just as well.

00:45:54.310 --> 00:45:55.390
Oh, please, no pictures.

00:45:56.030 --> 00:45:57.630
This is for the house collection, sir.

00:46:01.150 --> 00:46:03.330
That's going to look as if the drinks weren't very good.

00:46:04.080 --> 00:46:05.500
Maybe they can paint in a smile.

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:06.380
You're through.

00:46:06.940 --> 00:46:07.200
Sure.

00:46:07.440 --> 00:46:08.180
Let's get out of here.

00:46:08.790 --> 00:46:09.510
Got the change.

00:46:20.600 --> 00:46:21.480
Did you see the show tonight?

00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:22.580
Most of it.

00:46:22.820 --> 00:46:23.280
Like it?

00:46:25.150 --> 00:46:25.370
You.

00:46:26.280 --> 00:46:28.140
Didn't you think the boy with the harp was good?

00:46:28.300 --> 00:46:29.920
I, uh, did.

00:46:30.120 --> 00:46:31.580
I was waiting for you.

00:46:32.880 --> 00:46:34.480
Well, I won't be long.

00:46:35.580 --> 00:46:36.740
I'll pardon your back.

00:46:37.310 --> 00:46:37.490
What?

00:46:38.170 --> 00:46:39.900
About face, prosecutor.

00:46:40.710 --> 00:46:41.450
Oh, good.

00:46:45.280 --> 00:46:47.780
Is this visit, um, business or pleasure?

00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:51.110
Right now, it's your business and my pleasure.

00:46:52.040 --> 00:46:53.120
We can go somewhere else.

00:46:53.970 --> 00:46:55.890
People always want to go somewhere else.

00:46:58.300 --> 00:46:58.960
Do you blame them?

00:46:59.690 --> 00:46:59.970
Fancy.

00:47:01.210 --> 00:47:02.930
This wall is very uninteresting.

00:47:05.690 --> 00:47:06.650
Patience, patience.

00:47:07.860 --> 00:47:08.920
I'm changing my mind.

00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:10.040
About what?

00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:11.360
About you.

00:47:13.010 --> 00:47:14.190
All right, Addie.

00:47:18.270 --> 00:47:19.090
Changing from what?

00:47:19.410 --> 00:47:19.490
What?

00:47:21.010 --> 00:47:23.670
From maybe, perhaps.

00:47:24.890 --> 00:47:26.590
Are you always so uncertain about things?

